1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,350
This pond has killed at least ten divers.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,960
From above, it's just a pond in the woods.

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:08,590
Below, a narrow shaft called the Chimney drops into the dark.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,080
Then it opens into a huge room divers call the Ballroom.

5
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:13,870
Florida's Eagle's Nest.

6
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:16,830
Divers call it the Mount Everest of cave diving.

7
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:21,410
The cave runs on past the Ballroom, to about 300 feet deep.

8
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:25,590
120 feet down, there's a sign with the Grim Reaper on it.

9
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:26,460
It reads:

10
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:26,780
Stop.

11
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:27,770
Prevent your death.

12
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:28,790
Go no farther.

13
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:34,060
In 1999, partly over safety fears, it was closed to divers.

14
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,190
Cave divers pushed back.

15
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:38,140
It reopened in 2003.

16
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:40,200
October 2016.

17
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,250
Three friends came to dive it.

18
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,990
One stayed near the surface.

19
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:46,340
Two experienced divers went deep.

20
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,120
They were due back within an hour.

21
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:49,290
They never surfaced.

22
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:54,840
Recovery divers found them the next morning, around 260 feet down.

23
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,260
Exactly what went wrong is still unclear.

24
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,910
And from above, it still looks like a pond.
